cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: apok-eval
abstract: >-
  apok-eval is a verification-first evaluator of spiral fits for the Vesuvius Challenge. It scores a spiral
  fit, a set of tifxyz winding surfaces, against human fibre traces the fit did not use (E7 v3): per-family
  offsets are calibrated on one half of the fibres and the other half is scored against z-offset and rotation
  nulls. A CT positive control first checks that the fibres lie on the scan's papyrus layers, a ceiling reports
  the score a perfect fit could reach with the same fibres, and an optional leakage audit scores the fibre
  points away from the fit's own inputs. Every run is sealed in a record of every byte read, every setting and
  the code's identity, which anyone can re-check, and an optional licence gate refuses to read any input that
  is not declared with a licence whose required terms the user has accepted. The repository contains no scroll
  data and no results on scroll data.
authors:
  - name: Static Signal Ltd
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LaBlueberryPie/apok-eval"
url: "https://github.com/LaBlueberryPie/apok-eval"
keywords:
  - Vesuvius Challenge
  - Herculaneum papyri
  - virtual unwrapping
  - spiral fitting
  - evaluation
  - computed tomography
  - OME-Zarr
